## What the official site says

[Rockstar’s GTA VI page](https://www.rockstargames.com/VI), checked on 18 November 2026, still says the game is coming November 19, 2026 for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. The page shows **Pre-Load Now**, and it still labels PlayStation 5 as the platform it plays best on. That page does not list a PC date.

Treat November 19 as Rockstar’s stated target, not a promise that the date cannot move. If it changes, the change belongs on Rockstar’s page.

This is a separate game from Grand Theft Auto V Enhanced, which is already released on PC. The Enhanced edition has its own [Steam listing](/apps/gta-v-enhanced).

## Who can pre-load now

Pre-loading is no longer a future November 10 start. Rockstar’s [Pre-Load Grand Theft Auto VI Now](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/89834o94713o21/pre-load-grand-theft-auto-vi-now) post, dated 10 November 2026 and still linked from the GTA VI page on 18 November 2026, says pre-loading is available for everyone who has pre-ordered digitally. The same post says players who pre-ordered the code-in-box version can activate that code and begin pre-loading as soon as the code is received.

| Platform | What the official sources say |
| --- | --- |
| PlayStation 5 | [PlayStation’s 10 November 2026 post](https://blog.playstation.com/2026/11/10/pre-load-grand-theft-auto-vi-on-ps5-starting-today/), rechecked 18 November 2026, says pre-loading is available at PlayStation Store. It also says code-in-box buyers can activate the code as soon as they get it. |
| Xbox Series X\|S | [Xbox Wire’s 10 November 2026 post](https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/11/10/grand-theft-auto-6-comes-to-xbox-cloud-gaming-november-19/), rechecked 18 November 2026, says Series X and Series S native installs are available now to pre-install, and it encourages players to begin early for launch day. |
| Xbox One | The same Xbox Wire post, rechecked 18 November 2026, says Xbox One plays the game through Xbox Cloud Gaming. It does not describe a native Xbox One install. |
| PC | Rockstar’s GTA VI page still does not list a PC release. There is no PC pre-load to start from that page. |

Rockstar’s earlier [Pre-Load Begins on November 10](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/k4ak9okk485712) headline marked the start of that window. Use the newer **Pre-Load Now** post and your console store for the current download button.

## How release timing works

Rockstar’s page keeps November 19, 2026 as the launch day for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S.

PlayStation’s 10 November 2026 post, rechecked 18 November 2026, says launch unlocks on a rolling midnight by country, beginning at 12:00 a.m. NZDT in New Zealand on November 19 and continuing as other countries reach midnight. Pre-loading installs the game files early. It does not unlock play before that launch window.

Xbox Wire’s 10 November 2026 post, rechecked 18 November 2026, says Xbox Cloud Gaming play for Xbox One and Xbox Series X|S begins at 1 a.m. ET on November 19. A Series X or Series S native install is separate from cloud streaming.

Rockstar publishes a [platforms and editions support article](https://support.rockstargames.com/articles/4QfG4FmZCf5W1gS8jy4UVT/grand-theft-auto-vi-platform-editions-and-versions). A fresh fetch of that support page failed during this check, so use Rockstar’s page directly for the current wording on physical editions and retail codes. Retail shipping and pickup timing can vary by store.

## What this page does not claim

This page does not quote a required download size. Rockstar’s current GTA VI page and the Pre-Load Now post checked here do not state a gigabyte figure, so none is invented.

This is a dated editorial snapshot. It is not a hands-on preview, a PC release date, or a performance comparison. GameNews is not affiliated with Rockstar. When a newer official post appears, use the publisher’s page rather than an older recap.
